1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,312
My smart speaker just told me to cancel tonight's flight, using a voice I have never heard before.

2
00:00:06,612 --> 00:00:15,084
Leo, twenty-eight, in the same gray hoodie, touches the speaker, demanding to know who spoke inside his locked apartment.

3
00:00:15,384 --> 00:00:21,888
The device does not answer with silence. It plays back the sound of my own panic from tomorrow morning.

4
00:00:22,188 --> 00:00:31,524
Leo, wearing his gray hoodie, paces across the wooden floorboards, realizing the timestamp on the file reads four hours ahead.

5
00:00:31,824 --> 00:00:38,016
I try to unplug the machine, but the cord vanishes into my own hand like smoke in the wind.

6
00:00:38,316 --> 00:00:46,500
Leo, still trapped in the gray hoodie, hears the front door handle jiggle violently as someone tries to break in.

7
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:54,408
The speaker whispers my exact final words, begging for mercy against an intruder who looks just like me.

8
00:00:54,708 --> 00:01:02,628
Leo, holding his breath in the gray hoodie, sees the lock snap open and the darkness flood inside the room.

9
00:01:02,928 --> 00:01:10,104
The terrifying truth hits me: the past can be changed, but the future has already buried us.

10
00:01:10,404 --> 00:01:17,124
If your final words were already recorded right now, would you still bother saying anything at all?
